## Objective
- Implement `phase-100` in `/home/runner/work/rbops/rbops/redblue`: add a platform-aware `path` value/module (`join`, `parent`, `filename`, `stem`, `extension`, `is_absolute`, `resolve`, directory listing) and route `files.*` through it while preserving string-path compatibility.
- Add tests, docs, `REPORT.md`, and pass all four gates.

## Important Details
- Working directory is the only allowed read/write area: `/home/runner/work/rbops/rbops/redblue`.
- Do not inspect or modify `../rbops/`; do not touch `.github/workflows/`, `rbops/`, `.opencode/agent/`, or `rbops/phases.json`.
- `must_touch: [src/]`; phase fails without a changed file under `src/`.
- Never weaken/delete existing tests or add ignores/skips/suppressions.
- Required gate order:
  - `cargo fmt --all -- --check`
  - `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`
  - `cargo test --all-targets`
  - `../rbops/verify.sh "phase-100"` (project has no local `rbops/`; prompt also mentions `./rbops/verify.sh phase-100`)
- Path value design chosen: `Value::Object("path", {text: ...})`, no new `Value` variant.
  - Constants: `src/path.rs::OBJECT_NAME = "path"`, `TEXT_FIELD = "text"`.
  - Prints as its text; `type_of` answers `"path"`; compares equal to its text; hash is special-cased to `HASH_TEXT`.
- `path.join`, `path.parent`, `path.resolve` return path values; `filename`, `stem`, `extension` return text or `nothing`; `is_absolute` returns yes/no; `path.list` returns sorted text names.
- Separators come from `std::path::MAIN_SEPARATOR`; `join_with_separator` exists for POSIX/Windows tests.
- `files.read/write/append/exists/lines/delete/copy/rename` now accept either `Value::Text` or a path value via `path::text_of`.

